From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:22:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: RRC null integrity (EIA0) detector
 (T-OR-111 part a)

RrcNullIntegrityAnalyzer (default off) flags an RRC configuration that
selects the null integrity algorithm (EIA0), leaving access-stratum
signalling unauthenticated -- the AS-layer counterpart to the NAS EIA0 that
null_integrity catches. A UE that accepts it will act on forged RRC
(measurement config, reconfiguration, release/redirect), the foothold a
false base station needs. High.

The AS can select the integrity algorithm in two places, and both are
checked: a SecurityModeCommand (securityConfigSMC), and a handover
RRCConnectionReconfiguration (securityConfigHO -- intra-LTE or inter-RAT),
since a handover establishes AS algorithms without a separate Security Mode
Command and a CSS could select EIA0 there too.

The one legitimate use of EIA0 is an unauthenticated emergency call;
suppressing that case needs connection state and is the remaining stateful
part of T-OR-111, so an emergency call is a known false positive until then
-- hence off by default.

Test vectors are DL-DCCH PDUs encoded with the reference Python pycrate and
decoded through telcom_parser: a Security Mode Command selecting EIA0, an
intra-LTE and an inter-RAT handover reconfiguration selecting EIA0 (all fire
High), the same with EIA2 and a reconfiguration without securityConfigHO
(ignored), a DLInformationTransfer (ignored), and a non-LTE element.

